To assess the effectiveness of the RL-based time slot selection method for devices requesting fresh global models, we compare it against three baseline strategies. The first hypothesis (H1) involves the device sending the request immediately after the first local epoch. The second hypothesis (H2) has the device sending the request midway through local training, while the third hypothesis (H3) dictates that the request is made in the penultimate local epoch. Our RL approach demonstrates a marked improvement in accuracy over these baselines, outperforming H1 by 2.4\%, H2 by 2.2\%, and H3 by 2.8\%.

