\add{In conclusion,} the global-regularity of solutions of 3D hydrodynamical PDEs, such as the 3D IMHD equations, continues to challenge physicists, fluid dynamicists, and mathematicians. Numerical studies play an important role in the quest for FTSs 
in such PDEs. We have taken the first crucial step that is required for uncovering FTSs in the 3D IMHD equations: In particular, we have presented compelling numerical evidence for the development of (potential) finite-time singularities in these equations in a wall-bounded axisymmetric domain. Furthermore, we have obtained deep insights into these FTSs by examining secondary flows and their dependence on the effective pressure $P$ \add{at initial times}.

