Any practical implementation of a pseudospectral DNS has a finite spatial resolution, so the extraction of $\delta$ can only be accurate up until the time at which the spectral approximation is relatively free from errors~\cite{kolluru2024novel}; 
beyond this time, spectral convergence is lost, so we stop our analysis. For the 3DAE~\cite{kolluru2022insights} and for the 3D-axisymmetric IMHD flows that we discuss here, we see the emergence of localised oscillatory structures, called \textit{tygers}~\cite{tyger1}, around this time; at later times, the energy spectra show signs of thermalization~\cite{cichowlas2005effective,di2018dynamics,kolluru2022insights}.
