   For sufficiently small $\delta>0$, the metric $g_\delta=\delta^2 g_1$ has scalar curvature $\scal_{g_\delta} \geq S_0$ and $(M\setminus \{\text{point}\},g_\delta)$ contains an isometric copy of $[0,\infty)\times \S^{n-1}_\delta$.
   Given $l>0$ we can cut the cylinder $[0,\infty)\times \S^{n-1}_\delta$ at $l$.
