In this paper, we propose a family of novel monotonic post-hoc calibration maps that perform Instance-Wise Monotonic Calibration by Constrained Transformation (MCCT). By applying constrained transformations to sorted logits, the proposed method enables an interpretable and parameterized transformation while ensuring a robust and expressive calibration map that remains strictly monotonic. Implementing the calibration map through constrained optimization allows the model to learn a calibration map in an efficient and data-effective manner. Extensive experiments on CIFAR-10, CIFAR-100, and ImageNet demonstrate that our proposed methods, MCCT and its variant MCCT-I, outperform the existing state-of-the-art calibration methods. The source code is available at \url{https://github.com/YunruiZhang/Calibration-by-Constrained-Transformation}

